00:02:50.460 --> 00:02:55.260
A price can work as a forecast and how it works is easiest to see in the old presidential

00:02:55.260 --> 00:02:55.980
betting markets.

00:02:56.580 --> 00:03:03.000
From 1868 to 1940, large and often well-organized markets took wagers on who would win the White

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:03.300
House.

00:03:03.960 --> 00:03:08.280
Buyers took a claim that paid if their candidate won and sellers took the other side.

00:03:08.280 --> 00:03:12.560
The trading level was the forecast because that was where people were willing to risk

00:03:12.560 --> 00:03:15.040
money, not because anyone had run a poll.

00:03:15.620 --> 00:03:20.620
A 2004 article in the Journal of Economic Perspectives studies those markets and sets out

00:03:20.620 --> 00:03:21.340
four findings.

00:03:21.780 --> 00:03:25.900
They did a remarkable job calling elections before scientific polling existed.

00:03:26.440 --> 00:03:30.960
They were fairly efficient even though participants had limited information and even though people

00:03:30.960 --> 00:03:32.980
actively tried to manipulate the odds.

00:03:33.420 --> 00:03:38.060
They largely disappeared the paper argues because scientific polls rose and because other

00:03:38.060 --> 00:03:43.480
gambling became easier to find. The paper also discusses lessons for the present, and the

00:03:43.480 --> 00:03:48.860
abstract does not itemize them. That second finding is the caution. Efficiency is claimed

00:03:48.860 --> 00:03:54.980
next to manipulation, not instead of it. A push can fail if other traders take the other

00:03:54.980 --> 00:04:00.100
side, and a price can still miss if the people trading share a blind spot. The abstract

00:04:00.100 --> 00:04:05.160
never measures how hard a price had to be shoved before it broke. For anyone reading a contract

00:04:05.160 --> 00:04:08.420
track now, the number is only the level at which someone risked money.

00:04:08.940 --> 00:04:13.520
Under that venue's rules for who gets paid, those old markets show a price can track

00:04:13.520 --> 00:04:18.140
an election before polls exist, and that the markets themselves can fade once polls

00:04:18.140 --> 00:04:19.980
and other wagers are easier to use.

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:23.180
They do not turn any single price today into a verdict.

